{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3816999","formula":"Na₂Mg₄Cr₂(Si₆O₁₈)O₂","hill":"Cr2Mg4Na2O20Si6","elements":["O","Na","Mg","Si","Cr"],"composition":{"O":20.0,"Cr":2.0,"Mg":4.0,"Na":2.0,"Si":6.0},"names":{"en":"Krinovite","uk":"Кріновіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Krinovite (pronounced kreen'-off-ite) is an emerald-green triclinic meteorite mineral, containing chromium, magnesium, oxygen, silicon, and sodium, of the aenigmatite group. \"It has been discovered within graphite nodules in three iron meteorites,\" specifically the Canyon Diablo, Wichita County, and Youndegin meteorites. It was named in honour of Evgeny Leonidovich Krinov, Russian investigator of meteorites.","uk":"Кріновіт — смарагдово-зелений триклінний метеоритний мінерал, що містить хром, магній, кисень, кремній і натрій, з групи енігматиту. Він був виявлений у графітових конкреціях у трьох залізних метеоритах, а саме: у метеоритах «Canyon Diablo», «Wichita County» та «Youndegin». Названий на честь Євгена Леонідовича Крінова, російського дослідника метеоритів."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3816999","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krinovite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9A%D1%80%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krinovite.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q423010","formula":"Mg₂Si₂O₆","names":{"en":"Enstatite","ru":"Энстатит","uk":"Енстатит"},"elements":["O","Mg","Si"],"fame":35,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q75149